  "summary": "Streamline traditional East African flavors with this fast <b>Ethiopian roasted chicken</b> recipe tailored specifically for busy weeknights. Bone-in chicken thighs are coated in a vibrant glaze of aromatic <b>berbere spice blend</b>, garlic, ginger, and rich clarified butter before roasting. Placed over a layer of sliced red onions, the meat juices and spices drip down during baking to create tender caramelized onions infused with flavor. Roasting at high heat yields delightfully crispy skin while keeping the chicken juicy and succulent inside. This simplified one-pan method captures the essence of classic slow-cooked stews like Doro Wat in under forty minutes of total kitchen time. Serve this comforting dish with tangy injera flatbread or warm flatbreads to soak up the fragrant pan drippings. It provides a thrilling, spice-packed dinner option that brings authentic flavor to your table without needing hours of stove monitoring.",
